19:T5f6,## Open for extension, closed for modification

The **O** in SOLID. A module should let you add new behaviour **without editing the code that already works**. You extend by **writing new code**, not by reopening tested code and risking the bugs that come with it.

## The smell: `if/else` on a type

The tell-tale sign is a method that switches on *what kind of thing* it has:

```
double area(Shape s){
    if      (s is Circle) return PI*r*r;
    else if (s is Rect)   return w*h;
    // add Triangle? EDIT here  ← reopen tested code
}
```

Every new shape forces you back into this **one** method. You touch code that already passed its tests, re-review it, re-deploy it, and the bug surface grows with each `else if`. The class is **closed to nothing**; it's reopened constantly.

## Invert it with an abstraction

Hide the variation behind an **interface**. Each kind of behaviour becomes its **own class** that the existing code never names:

```
interface Shape { double area(); }
double total(List<Shape> shapes){
    double t = 0;
    for (Shape s : shapes) t += s.area();   // never says "Circle"
    return t;
}
```

A new `Triangle` is a **new class** implementing `Shape`. `AreaCalculator` never sees it and never changes, it's **closed** to modification yet **open** to extension.

> This rests on **polymorphism** (one call, many forms) and on **LSP**, every `Shape` must be substitutable. It's also the same inversion as **DIP**: the high-level calculator depends on the abstraction, not the concrete shapes.c:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex min-h-screen","children":[["$","$L17",null,{"activeModule":"lld-solid","activeLesson":"open-closed"}],["$","$L18","open-closed",{"lesson":{"id":"open-closed","patternId":"lld-solid","title":"Open / Closed (O)","kind":"concept","difficulty":"Core","statement":"Software should be OPEN for extension but CLOSED for modification, add new behaviour by adding code, not by editing code that already works.","companies":["Amazon","Microsoft","Stripe"],"theory":"$19","approaches":[{"label":"Editing for every new type","code":["double area(Shape s){","    if      (s is Circle) return PI*r*r;","    else if (s is Rect)   return w*h;","    // add Triangle? EDIT here","}"],"steps":[{"view":"class","codeLine":1,"narration":"AreaCalculator computes area with a type-switch INSIDE the method, it inspects what kind of shape it was handed.","classDiagram":{"classes":[{"id":"calc","name":"AreaCalculator","methods":["+ area(s): double"],"x":1,"y":0.5,"tint":"red"}],"relations":[],"shownClassIds":["calc"],"shownRelIds":[],"activeIds":["calc"]},"vars":[["shape kinds","inside one method"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":2,"narration":"It works today: an if for Circle, an else-if for Rectangle. Two cases, two branches, all good so far.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":[],"shownClassIds":["calc"],"shownRelIds":[],"activeIds":["calc"]},"vars":[["handles","Circle + Rectangle"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":4,"narration":"Now you need Triangle. There is nowhere to add it except by REOPENING this tested method and wiring another else-if. The class is chained to every shape that exists.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":[],"shownClassIds":["calc"],"shownRelIds":[],"activeIds":["calc"]},"vars":[["new type","edit existing code 💥"]]}]},{"label":"Extend without editing","code":["interface Shape { double area(); }","","class AreaCalculator {","    double total(List<Shape> shapes){","        double t = 0;","        for (Shape s : shapes) t += s.area();   // never names a type","        return t;","    }","}"],"steps":[{"view":"class","codeLine":1,"narration":"Introduce a Shape interface. AreaCalculator just sums shape.area() over a list, it never names a concrete type, so it never needs to know which shapes exist.","classDiagram":{"classes":[{"id":"shape","name":"Shape","stereotype":"interface","methods":["+ area(): double"],"x":1,"y":0.2,"tint":"accent"},{"id":"calc","name":"AreaCalculator","methods":["+ total(shapes)"],"x":0,"y":0.2},{"id":"circle","name":"Circle","methods":["+ area()"],"x":0.3,"y":1.6},{"id":"rect","name":"Rectangle","methods":["+ area()"],"x":1.3,"y":1.6},{"id":"tri","name":"Triangle","methods":["+ area()"],"x":2.3,"y":1.6,"tint":"green"}],"relations":[{"id":"d","from":"calc","to":"shape","kind":"depend","label":"calls area()"},{"id":"c","from":"circle","to":"shape","kind":"implement"},{"id":"r","from":"rect","to":"shape","kind":"implement"},{"id":"t","from":"tri","to":"shape","kind":"implement"}],"shownClassIds":["shape","calc"],"shownRelIds":["d"],"activeIds":["calc"]},"vars":[["calculator","sums area()"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":1,"narration":"Circle and Rectangle each implement Shape, giving area() their own body. The calculator already works with both, and never mentioned either by name.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["shape","calc","circle","rect"],"shownRelIds":["d","c","r"],"activeIds":["circle","rect"]}},{"view":"class","narration":"Need Triangle? Add it as a NEW class implementing Shape. It slots straight into the same loop. AreaCalculator is NOT touched, not one line.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["shape","calc","circle","rect","tri"],"shownRelIds":["d","c","r","t"],"activeIds":["tri"]},"vars":[["add Triangle","0 edits to calculator ✓"]]},{"view":"class","narration":"Open for extension, new behaviour arrives as new classes. Closed for modification, the existing, tested calculator stays untouched. That is the Open/Closed Principle.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["shape","calc","circle","rect","tri"],"shownRelIds":["d","c","r","t"],"activeIds":["shape","calc"]},"vars":[["extend","add classes"],["existing code","untouched ✓"]]}]}]}}]]}]
